1,2$ Fruitbodies hyaline to whitish, occasionally tinted pink to violaceous
1,3$ Fruitbodies distinctly coloured, orange, brown or black
2,0$ (1) Mature fruitbodies whitish; effused, becoming plicate; no mineral inclusions; basidia not stalked $ thuretiana
2,0$ Mature fruitbodies hyaline to whitish, occasionally tinted pink to violaceous; pustular and coalescing; white mineral inclusions often visible; basidia distinctly stalked $ nucleata
3,4$ (1) Fruitbodies blackish-brown to black; hymenium with scattered warts or papillae under lens
3,5$ Fruitbodies orange to brown; hymenium smooth
4,0$ (3) Fruitbodies turbinate, often remaining separate, occasionally coalescing; typically on oak or hazel $ glandulosa
4,0$ Fruitbodies effused, irregularly lobed, coalescing; typically on beech, willow, sycamore and other deciduous trees (but rarely, if ever, on oak) $ plana
5,0$ Fruitbodies brown, irregularly lobed; on pine $ saccharina
5,6$ Fruitbodies ornage to orange-brown; on deciduous trees
6,0$ Fruitbodies button-shaped; typically on birch $ repanda
